1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,369
Hitler sent a panzer division to the wrong country... because of the man in this grave.

2
00:00:05,529 --> 00:00:09,496
There's just one problem. Major William Martin never existed.

3
00:00:09,656 --> 00:00:16,284
April 1943. A body in a British officer's uniform washes up on this beach in Spain.

4
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:20,076
Chained to his coat: a briefcase of top secret letters.

5
00:00:21,135 --> 00:00:24,015
They revealed the Allies' next target. Greece.

6
00:00:24,175 --> 00:00:27,810
Spain was neutral. But it was crawling with German spies.

7
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:32,214
Within weeks, the letters reached Hitler's headquarters. And he believed them.

8
00:00:32,374 --> 00:00:34,652
German forces were rushed to Greece.

9
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:39,469
Then, on July 10th, 1943, the Allies landed somewhere else.

10
00:00:40,179 --> 00:00:40,980
Sicily.

11
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:46,838
The officer was pure fiction. His fiancée. His love letters. Even his theatre tickets.

12
00:00:46,998 --> 00:00:52,957
But the body was real. A homeless Welshman who died in London, and was forgotten for fifty years.

13
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:57,114
So who was he? And how did two British officers pull this off?

14
00:00:57,274 --> 00:00:59,589
